 * `inset-inline-start/-end: var(--ant-margin-sm)`). The footer's `left: 50%` plus
 * `translateX(-50%)` centering made it the containing block of its switches, which then sat
 * over the toolbar's ends. The footer is centered with auto margins instead (no transform),
 * so the switches can be fixed to the viewport sides like v6's own.
 */
.ant-image-preview .ant-image-preview-footer {
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  width: fit-content;
  margin-inline: auto;
  transform: none;
}
.ant-image-preview .ant-image-preview-footer .ant-image-preview-switch {
  position: fixed;
}

/*
 * The action list's DOM order is v4's: close, zoomIn, zoomOut, rotateRight, rotateLeft, flipX,
 * flipY. v4 lays it out with `flex-direction: row-reverse`, so the actions read flipY, flipX,
 * rotateLeft, rotateRight, zoomOut, zoomIn left-to-right with close at the trailing end. That is
 * antd v6's own action order (`Preview/Footer.js` renders flipY first and zoomIn last), so the
 * reversal is kept, and set here for when only the v6 bundle is loaded, instead of reading the
 * list in source order. The progress counter is the list's first item; `order` keeps it at the
 * leading end of the pill, where it sits in source order, and stays on one line when a wide
 * custom actions template squeezes the pill.
 */
.ant-image-preview-actions {
  flex-direction: row-reverse;
}
.ant-image-preview-actions > .ant-image-preview-operations-progress {
  order: 1;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/*
 * v4 spaces action items with `margin-left` on each `li`; v6 uses `gap` on the actions
 * container instead. Both are additive (nothing removes the `gap`), so the per-item
 * margin is cleared to avoid doubled spacing between actions.
 */
.ant-image-preview-actions-action {
  margin-left: 0;
  margin-inline-start: 0;
}

/*
 * v6 draws the previewed image's `max-height: 70%` against `.ant-image-preview-body`'s own
 * `position: absolute; inset: 0` (a definite height). ng-zorro additionally nests the image in
 * `.ant-image-preview-img-wrapper` for the drag handle; v4's own `position: absolute; inset: 0`
 * on that wrapper (needed for the same definite-height chain) is a v4-only rule with no v6
 * counterpart, so it is mirrored here for the case where only the v6 bundle is loaded (no v4
 * stylesheet) -- without it the wrapper falls back to a static, content-sized box, the `70%`
 * percentage has no definite containing-block height to resolve against, and the image renders
 * unconstrained at its intrinsic size instead of fitted inside the viewport.
 *
 * v6 centres the image by making `.ant-image-preview-body` itself `display: flex;
 * align-items: center; justify-content: center` and rendering the <img> as its direct flex
 * child. ng-zorro's `-img-wrapper` sits between body and the image (for the drag handle) and is
 * not a flex container, so the image -- sized by the rule above -- sits at the wrapper's
 * top-left corner instead of centred. v4's own centring technique (an inline-block `::before`
 * ghost element plus `vertical-align: middle`) only works with the wrapper NOT absolutely
 * positioned the way this rule positions it, so it is not reusable here; centring the wrapper's
 * own content with flex is the minimum additional rule that reaches the same visual result.
 */
.ant-image-preview-img-wrapper {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
}

/*
 * v6's `.ant-image-preview .ant-image-preview-close` rule assumes `close` is a direct child of
 * `.ant-image-preview` (`Preview/index.js` renders `CloseBtn` as a sibling of `Footer`, not nested
 * inside it) and positions it absolutely in the top-right corner with its own circular,
 * semi-transparent badge. ng-zorro keeps `close` as the first action inside the v4 toolbar
 * (moving it out would change the v4-rendered markup), where that absolute corner-positioning
 * instead draws the badge over the action pill's own corner. Rather than attempt antd's separate
 * top-right placement, `close` is laid out as an ordinary pill action here: positioning is
 * neutralised back to the normal flex-item flow, and its background/radius are reset to the
 * transparent, square-cornered look `.ant-image-preview-actions-action`'s siblings already have
 * (padding is already identical, so it is left alone). Equal specificity to the base
 * `.ant-image-preview .ant-image-preview-close` rule (two classes each); this rule wins on
 * source order, the same way every other neutraliser in this file does.
 */
.ant-image-preview-footer .ant-image-preview-close {
  position: static;
  top: auto;
  inset-inline-end: auto;
  background-color: transparent;
  border-radius: 0;
}
.ant-image-preview-footer .ant-image-preview-close:hover,
.ant-image-preview-footer .ant-image-preview-close:active {
  background-color: transparent;
}
textarea.nz-textarea-autosize-measuring {
  height: auto !important;
  padding: 2px 0 !important;
  overflow: hidden !important;
}

nz-form-item-feedback-icon.ant-input-suffix {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  inset-inline-end: 0;
  z-index: 1;
  display: flex;
  flex: none;
  align-items: center;
  height: 100%;
  margin-inline-start: var(--ant-input-affix-margin, 4px);
  margin-inline-end: var(--ant-padding-sm);
  pointer-events: none;
}

.ant-input-status-error.ant-input-has-feedback,
.ant-input-status-warning.ant-input-has-feedback,
.ant-input-status-validating.ant-input-has-feedback,
.ant-input-status-success.ant-input-has-feedback {
  padding-inline-end: calc(var(--ant-padding-lg) + var(--ant-padding-xxs));
}

.ant-input-textarea-show-count {
  position: relative;
  display: block;
}

.ant-input-stepperless[type='number'] {
  -moz-appearance: textfield;
}

.ant-input-stepperless[type='number']::-webkit-inner-spin-button,
.ant-input-stepperless[type='number'] ::-webkit-outer-spin-button {
  margin: 0;
  -webkit-appearance: none;
}

.ant-otp-input {
  width: auto;
}
/*
 * antd v6's InputNumber never wraps prefix/suffix in an affix-wrapper element (rc-input-number
 * renders `-prefix`/`-suffix` as siblings of the input inside the single root div), so the
 * generated v6 CSS carries no display/width/border rule for `.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper`
 * beyond its `-lg`/`-sm` padding variants. ng-zorro keeps a real affix-wrapper element around the
 * `.ant-input-number` root for the default (v4) stylesheet, so it needs its own v6 layout: this
 * mirrors antd's `.ant-input-affix-wrapper` base rule (Input's own affix wrapper) onto it.
 */
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  width: var(--ant-input-number-control-width);
  min-width: 0;
  transition: all var(--ant-motion-duration-mid);
}

/* Only applies the default (medium) padding/radius: the real v6 `-affix-wrapper-lg`/`-sm` rules
   already set both at the same (single-class) specificity, so this is guarded to avoid winning
   ties against them by source order. */
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper:not(.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-lg):not(.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-sm) {
  padding: var(--ant-input-number-padding-block) var(--ant-input-number-padding-inline);
  border-radius: var(--ant-border-radius);
}

/*
 * Mirrors antd v6's `.ant-input-outlined` border/background states (Input's own outlined rule)
 * onto the affix wrapper: v6 never applies an outlined rule to a wrapper prefix, because Input's
 * `.ant-input-affix-wrapper` carries the border itself and InputNumber's inner root has no
 * second, separate wrapper element to draw it on in real v6 markup.
 */
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined {
  background: var(--ant-color-bg-container);
  border-width: var(--ant-line-width);
  border-style: var(--ant-line-type);
  border-color: var(--ant-color-border);
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined:hover {
  border-color: var(--ant-input-number-hover-border-color);
  background-color: var(--ant-input-number-hover-bg);
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined:focus-within,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-focused {
  border-color: var(--ant-input-number-active-border-color);
  box-shadow: var(--ant-input-number-active-shadow);
  background-color: var(--ant-input-number-active-bg);
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-disabled {
  color: var(--ant-color-text-disabled);
  background-color: var(--ant-color-bg-container-disabled);
  border-color: var(--ant-color-border-disabled);
  box-shadow: none;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-status-error {
  border-color: var(--ant-color-error);
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-status-error:hover {
  border-color: var(--ant-color-error-border-hover);
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-status-error:focus-within {
  border-color: var(--ant-color-error);
  box-shadow: var(--ant-input-number-error-active-shadow);
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-status-warning {
  border-color: var(--ant-color-warning);
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-status-warning:hover {
  border-color: var(--ant-color-warning-border-hover);
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-status-warning:focus-within {
  border-color: var(--ant-color-warning);
  box-shadow: var(--ant-input-number-warning-active-shadow);
}

.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper-rtl {
  direction: rtl;
}

/*
 * Neutralises the inner root's own border/background/shadow so it is not drawn a second time
 * inside the wrapper's border box, mirroring v4's `affix.less` "> div.ant-input-number
 * { border: none; outline: none; }" rule for the v6 stylesheet. Each selector repeats the state
 * (`:hover`/`:focus-within`/disabled/status) of the v6 rule it neutralises with one extra class
 * (the wrapper ancestor), so it always outranks that rule's specificity regardless of source
 * order, per the specificity-matching rule used for the checkbox/radio box patches.
 */
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number {
  width: 100%;
  border: none;
  outline: none;
  background: transparent;
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined:hover,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined:focus,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined:focus-within,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined.ant-input-number-disabled,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined.ant-input-number-status-error,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined.ant-input-number-status-error:hover,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined.ant-input-number-status-error:focus,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined.ant-input-number-status-error:focus-within,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined.ant-input-number-status-warning,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined.ant-input-number-status-warning:hover,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined.ant-input-number-status-warning:focus,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined.ant-input-number-status-warning:focus-within {
  background: transparent;
  border-color: transparent;
  box-shadow: none;
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined:focus,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper > .ant-input-number-outlined:focus-within {
  outline: 0;
}

/* Mirrors antd v6's `.ant-input-affix-wrapper .ant-input-prefix/-suffix` spacing. */
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper .ant-input-number-prefix,
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper .ant-input-number-suffix {
  display: flex;
  flex: none;
  align-items: center;
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper .ant-input-number-prefix {
  margin-inline-end: var(--ant-padding-xxs);
}
.ant-input-number-affix-wrapper .ant-input-number-suffix {
  margin-inline-start: var(--ant-padding-xxs);
}

/*
 * antd v6 keeps its legacy `Input.Group` table/table-cell layout for back-compat (`.ant-input-group`,
 * `.ant-input-group-addon`, `.ant-input-group-wrapper*` in the generated v6 CSS), because
 * `addonBefore`/`addonAfter` are deprecated-but-supported props rendered through `Space.Compact` +
 * bare `-addon` spans, not through that legacy markup. ng-zorro's InputNumber still renders the
 * legacy `-group`/`-group-addon`/`-group-wrapper`/`-wrapper` DOM for the default (v4) stylesheet
 * (see the v6-api-gaps/allowlist notes), which has no v6 rule at all under its own
 * `ant-input-number-*` names. This mirrors that same legacy Input.Group table layout onto the
 * `ant-input-number-*` names, one property set at a time, so the addon renders as one row
 * (like `Input`'s own legacy addon demos still do in v6) instead of stacking as block-level divs.
 */
.ant-input-number-group {
  position: relative;
  display: table;
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: separate;
  border-spacing: 0;
}
.ant-input-number-group > .ant-input-number {
  display: table-cell;
}
.ant-input-number-group > .ant-input-number:not(:first-child):not(:last-child) {
  border-radius: 0;
}
.ant-input-number-group .ant-input-number-group-addon {
  position: relative;
  display: table-cell;
  width: 1px;
  padding: 0 var(--ant-input-number-padding-inline);
  color: var(--ant-color-text);
  font-weight: normal;
  text-align: center;
  white-space: nowrap;
  vertical-align: middle;
  border-radius: var(--ant-border-radius);
  transition: all var(--ant-motion-duration-slow);
  line-height: 1;
}
.ant-input-number-group .ant-input-number-group-addon:not(:first-child):not(:last-child) {
  border-radius: 0;
}
.ant-input-number-group > .ant-input-number:first-child,
.ant-input-number-group .ant-input-number-group-addon:first-child {
  border-start-end-radius: 0;
  border-end-end-radius: 0;
}
.ant-input-number-group > .ant-input-number:last-child,
.ant-input-number-group .ant-input-number-group-addon:last-child {
  border-start-start-radius: 0;
  border-end-start-radius: 0;
}

.ant-input-number-group-wrapper {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 100%;
  text-align: start;
  vertical-align: top;
}
.ant-input-number-group-wrapper-rtl {
  direction: rtl;
}
.ant-input-number-group-wrapper-outlined .ant-input-number-group-addon {
  background: var(--ant-input-number-addon-bg);
  border: var(--ant-line-width) var(--ant-line-type) var(--ant-color-border);
}
.ant-input-number-group-wrapper-outlined .ant-input-number-group-addon:first-child {
  border-inline-end: 0;
}
.ant-input-number-group-wrapper-outlined .ant-input-number-group-addon:last-child {
  border-inline-start: 0;
}
.ant-input-number-group-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-group-wrapper-status-error .ant-input-number-group-addon {
  border-color: var(--ant-color-error);
  color: var(--ant-color-error-text);
}
.ant-input-number-group-wrapper-outlined.ant-input-number-group-wrapper-status-warning
  .ant-input-number-group-addon {
  border-color: var(--ant-color-warning);
  color: var(--ant-color-warning-text);
}
/* Port of layout/style/patch.less: the nz-header/nz-content/nz-footer hosts are custom elements
   (inline by default); antd renders <header>/<main>/<footer>, which are block. */
nz-content,
nz-header,
nz-footer {
  display: block;
}
/* patch.less: nz-list, nz-list nz-spin, nz-list-header, nz-list-footer, nz-list-pagination,
   nz-list-empty, nz-list-item-extra { display: block } */
nz-list,
nz-list nz-spin,
nz-list-header,
nz-list-footer,
nz-list-pagination,
nz-list-empty,
nz-list-item-extra {
  display: block;
}
/* antd positions the dropdown with inline styles from rc-trigger (and hides it off-screen at
   `top:-9999px` before that); ng-zorro positions the CDK overlay pane itself instead, so the pane's own
   child needs a normal position in the flow. Port of `style/patch.less`'s `&-dropdown` rule; `margin-top`
   offsets the fixed `- 6` fudge factor `NzMentionComponent.updatePositions()` subtracts from the caret's
   line-bottom offset (so the two together clear the caret line the connected overlay is anchored to).
   `left`/`margin-bottom`/`width` tuned the box for the old (pre-CDK) inline layout and are dropped in
   favour of v6's own `padding`/`border-radius-lg` on the same element. */
.ant-mentions-dropdown {
  position: relative;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  inset-inline-start: 0;
  margin-top: 8px;
}
/* CDK overlay pane positioning: v6 sets `.ant-menu-submenu-popup { position: absolute }` (rc-trigger
   positions the popup itself), which would collapse the CDK pane that already places the popup next
   to its title. ng-zorro's popup root (`submenu-non-inline-child.component.ts`) carries
   `ant-menu-submenu ant-menu-submenu-popup` in both hosts, also when the submenu is nested in a
   `nz-dropdown-menu` (whose inner list carries dropdown's `ant-dropdown-menu*` classes instead), so the
   rule is not scoped to either. Port of `style/patch.less`'s `position: relative`. */
.ant-menu-submenu.ant-menu-submenu-popup {
  position: relative;
}

/* A horizontal popup's pane carries the title width as `min-width` (antd's `stretch: 'minWidth'` sets it
   on the popup itself). The pane is a flex container, so its popup root would stay content-wide inside
   it; letting it grow makes the list fill the pane. A pane without a min-width is as wide as its
   content, where this changes nothing. */
.cdk-overlay-pane > .ant-menu-submenu-popup:has(> .ant-menu) {
  flex-grow: 1;
}

/* Gap between the title and the popup. antd puts `paddingXS` on the popup root through rc-trigger's
   placement class (`.ant-menu-submenu-placement-rightTop` / `-leftTop` / `-bottomLeft`, ...), names
   ng-zorro does not emit: the compiled v4 stylesheet already styles `-placement-rightTop`, and ng-zorro
   keeps v4's coarse `-placement-right` / `-left` / `-bottom` (resolved from the CDK position in
   `submenu.component.ts`'s `onPositionChange`). This replaces `style/patch.less`'s `top: 6px` and
   `inset-inline-start` / `-end: 4px` offsets with v6's padding (the root's transparent `::before`
   covers the gap, so the pointer can cross it). Scoped to a menu-hosted popup (`> .ant-menu`): antd's
   dropdown submenu popup has no such padding, and `nz-dropdown-menu`'s nested popup keeps its v6
   geometry. Transform origin is set inline by the CDK (`cdkConnectedOverlayTransformOriginOn`). */
.ant-menu-submenu-popup.ant-menu-submenu-placement-right:has(> .ant-menu) {
  padding-inline-start: var(--ant-padding-xs);
}
.ant-menu-submenu-popup.ant-menu-submenu-placement-left:has(> .ant-menu) {
  padding-inline-end: var(--ant-padding-xs);
}
.ant-menu-submenu-popup.ant-menu-submenu-placement-bottom:has(> .ant-menu) {
  padding-top: var(--ant-padding-xs);
}

/* Collapsed inline menu: antd renders an item's icon BEFORE `.ant-menu-title-content`
   (`antd/es/menu/MenuItem.js`) and hides the title content with
   `.ant-menu-inline-collapsed > .ant-menu-item > .ant-menu-title-content { width: 0; opacity: 0;
   overflow: hidden }`. `[nz-menu-item]` projects its whole content, icon included, into that span
   (`menu-item.component.ts`), so the same rule would hide the icon too. When the title content holds
   an icon, `display: contents` drops its box (and with it the box-level `width`/`opacity`/`overflow`),
   so the icon and label become flex items of the collapsed `li` (`display: flex; align-items: center`)
   exactly as antd's are: the icon is centred by the item's own padding, and the label after it is still
   hidden by v6's `.ant-menu-inline-collapsed > .ant-menu-item .anticon + span` rule. Specificity is one
   class above each v6 selector it competes with (the item and the item-group-list item forms). Only an
   icon that is a direct child of the title content is detected: an icon nested in projected markup (an
   `<a>` wrapping `<nz-icon>` and its label) stays hidden with the title content under v6, as an antd
   item's label does (docs/v6-api-gaps.md). */
.ant-menu-inline-collapsed > .ant-menu-item > .ant-menu-title-content:has(> .anticon),
.ant-menu-inline-collapsed
  > .ant-menu-item-group
  > .ant-menu-item-group-list
  > .ant-menu-item
  > .ant-menu-title-content:has(> .anticon) {
  display: contents;
}

/* antd clones `ant-menu-item-icon` onto every item/submenu-title icon and styles it at
   `.ant-menu .ant-menu-item .ant-menu-item-icon { display: inline-flex; ... }` (0,3,0), which outranks the
   collapsed menu's `.ant-menu-inline-collapsed .anticon { display: inline-block }` (0,2,0). ng-zorro's
   `nz-icon` carries only `anticon` (`ant-menu-item-icon` is styled by the compiled v4 stylesheet, so it is
   not added), whose own `display: inline-flex` is (0,1,0) and loses: the icon would become a 40px-tall
   inline block with its glyph on the baseline. Mirror the display at the `-item-icon` rule's specificity;
   the other declarations of that rule match the global `.anticon` rule already. */
.ant-menu .ant-menu-item .anticon,
.ant-menu .ant-menu-submenu-title .anticon {
  display: inline-flex;
}

/* `[nz-menu-divider]` always renders dropdown's `ant-dropdown-menu-item-divider`
   (`menu-divider.directive.ts`); v6 styles that class only inside a dropdown (`.ant-dropdown
   .ant-dropdown-menu .ant-dropdown-menu-item-divider`), and the menu's own `ant-menu-item-divider` is
   styled by the compiled v4 stylesheet, so it is not added. Mirror of antd's
   `.ant-menu .ant-menu-item-divider` onto the divider of a plain menu. */
.ant-menu .ant-dropdown-menu-item-divider {
  overflow: hidden;
  line-height: 0;
  border-color: var(--ant-color-split);
  border-style: var(--ant-line-type);
  border-width: 0;
  border-top-width: var(--ant-line-width);
  margin-block: var(--ant-line-width);
  padding: 0;
}

/* `[nz-menu-divider nzDashed]` adds antd's `ant-menu-item-divider-dashed` next to the
   `ant-dropdown-menu-item-divider` the directive always renders. The divider mirror above sets
   `border-style: var(--ant-line-type)` at the specificity of v6's
   `.ant-menu .ant-menu-item-divider-dashed { border-style: dashed }` and later in the bundle, so the
   dashed style is repeated one class higher. */
.ant-menu .ant-dropdown-menu-item-divider.ant-menu-item-divider-dashed {
  border-style: dashed;
}

/* `nzExtra` on a dropdown-hosted item: v6 keys the layout on `.ant-dropdown-menu-title-content`, which
   the compiled v4 stylesheet styles, so ng-zorro keeps `.ant-menu-title-content` there
   (dropdown/style/v6/patch.css). Mirror of v6's `-title-content-with-extra` and `-item-extra` rules. */
.ant-dropdown-menu .ant-menu-title-content.ant-dropdown-menu-title-content-with-extra {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  width: 100%;
}
.ant-dropdown-menu .ant-menu-title-content .ant-dropdown-menu-item-extra {
  margin-inline-start: auto;
  padding-inline-start: var(--ant-padding);
  color: var(--ant-color-text-description);
  font-size: var(--ant-font-size-sm);
}
/* Motion, ported from components/message/style/animation.less. v6's message CSS is transition-based
   and defines no keyframes, but NzMNComponent adds ant-message-move-up-enter/-leave and removes the
   toast on `animationend`, so without these keyframes a toast is never removed. */
.ant-message .ant-message-move-up-enter,
.ant-message .ant-message-move-up-leave {
  animation-duration: var(--ant-motion-duration-slow);
  animation-timing-function: var(--ant-motion-ease-in-out-circ);
  animation-fill-mode: forwards;
}
.ant-message .ant-message-move-up-enter {
  animation-name: MessageMoveIn;
}
.ant-message .ant-message-move-up-leave {
  animation-name: MessageMoveOut;
}
@keyframes MessageMoveIn {
  0% {
    padding: 0;
    transform: translateY(-100%);
    opacity: 0;
  }
  100% {
    /* Ends at v6's rest padding (--ant-message-content-padding), so the toast does not snap to a
       different padding when the enter class is removed. */
    padding: var(--ant-message-content-padding);
    transform: translateY(0);
    opacity: 1;
  }
}
@keyframes MessageMoveOut {
  0% {
    max-height: 150px;
    /* Starts from the same rest padding, so the leave motion does not snap first. */
    padding: var(--ant-message-content-padding);
    opacity: 1;
  }
  100% {
    max-height: 0;
    padding: 0;
    opacity: 0;
  }
}

/* Mirrors `.ant-message .ant-message-list-content { gap: var(--ant-margin) }` onto the list root, since
   ng-zorro renders the toasts without the `-list-content` holder. v6's
   `.ant-message.ant-message-list { padding: var(--notification-margin-edge) }` (24px) would add to the
   container's inline top (nzTop), which in ng-zorro is the only vertical offset, as antd's
   `--notification-top` is, so the block-start padding is dropped. */
.ant-message.ant-message-list {
  gap: var(--ant-margin);
  padding-block-start: 0;
}

/* v6 `.ant-message .ant-message-notice { position: absolute }` assumes rc-notification's stacking,
   where JS offsets each toast with --notification-y. ng-zorro stacks the toasts in normal flow, so
   they stay relative (same selector, wins on source order). */
.ant-message .ant-message-notice {
  position: relative;
}

/* Mirrors `.ant-message.ant-message-top .ant-message-notice { left: 50%; transform: translate3d(-50%,
   0, 0) }` with `margin-inline: auto`: the MessageMoveIn/-Out keyframes set their own `transform`, which
   would override the v6 centring while they run. The shared keyframes stay free of a v6-only offset. */
.ant-message.ant-message-top .ant-message-notice {
  left: auto;
  transform: none;
  margin-inline: auto;
}

/* v6 lays out icon and title with `.ant-message-notice-wrapper { display: flex; align-items: center;
   gap }`. ng-zorro keeps v4's `.ant-message-custom-content` between the wrapper and the icon and title,
   so the flex row is mirrored onto it. Inert under v4, which gives it no `display`. */
.ant-message-notice-wrapper .ant-message-custom-content {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--ant-margin-xs);
}
/* antd v6 scopes most modal rules under `.ant-modal-root`, an element rc-dialog renders and ng-zorro
   does not: ng-zorro's containers carry `.ant-modal-wrap`/`.ant-modal` directly and the mask is the
   CDK backdrop. The `.ant-modal-root <selector>` rules are mirrored onto the bare selectors, except the
   min-width breakpoint `width` rules, which serve antd's responsive `width` object (no ng-zorro API).

   Mirrors `.ant-modal-root .ant-modal-mask`. */
.ant-modal-mask {
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: var(--ant-z-index-popup-base);
  height: 100%;
  background-color: var(--ant-color-bg-mask);
}

/* Mirrors `.ant-modal-root .ant-modal-wrap`: the fixed, full-viewport box the modal's `margin: 0 auto`
   centres in. */
.ant-modal-wrap {
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: var(--ant-z-index-popup-base);
  overflow: auto;
  outline: 0;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
}

/* Mirrors `.ant-modal-root .ant-modal-wrap-rtl{direction:rtl}` and
   `.ant-modal-root .ant-modal-wrap-rtl .ant-modal-confirm-body{direction:rtl}`. */
.ant-modal-wrap-rtl {
  direction: rtl;
}
.ant-modal-wrap-rtl .ant-modal-confirm-body {
  direction: rtl;
}

/* Mirrors the `.ant-modal-root .ant-modal-centered*` family (`nzCentered`). */
.ant-modal-centered {
  text-align: center;
}
.ant-modal-centered::before {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 0;
  height: 100%;
  vertical-align: middle;
  content: '';
}
.ant-modal-centered .ant-modal {
  top: 0;
  display: inline-block;
  padding-bottom: 0;
  text-align: start;
  vertical-align: middle;
}

/* Mirrors `.ant-modal-root .ant-modal.ant-zoom-enter/-appear` (fade in without the generic
   `.ant-zoom-enter` scale) and `.ant-modal-root .ant-modal.ant-zoom-leave .ant-modal-container`. */
.ant-modal.ant-zoom-enter,
.ant-modal.ant-zoom-appear {
  transform: none;
  opacity: 0;
  animation-duration: var(--ant-motion-duration-slow);
  user-select: none;
}
.ant-modal.ant-zoom-leave .ant-modal-container {
  pointer-events: none;
}

/* Mirrors the `.ant-modal-root .ant-fade-*` family for the backdrop, scoped to `.ant-modal-mask` so it
   does not reach other components' fade classes. */
.ant-modal-mask.ant-fade-enter,
.ant-modal-mask.ant-fade-appear {
  animation-duration: var(--ant-motion-duration-mid);
  animation-fill-mode: both;
  animation-play-state: paused;
  opacity: 0;
  animation-timing-function: linear;
}
.ant-modal-mask.ant-fade-leave {
  animation-duration: var(--ant-motion-duration-mid);
  animation-fill-mode: both;
  animation-play-state: paused;
  animation-timing-function: linear;
}
.ant-modal-mask.ant-fade-enter.ant-fade-enter-active,
.ant-modal-mask.ant-fade-appear.ant-fade-appear-active {
  animation-name: antFadeIn;
  animation-play-state: running;
}
.ant-modal-mask.ant-fade-leave.ant-fade-leave-active {
  animation-name: antFadeOut;
  animation-play-state: running;
  pointer-events: none;
}

/* antd v6 puts the confirm title and content in a flex-column `.ant-modal-confirm-paragraph` beside
   the icon. ng-zorro keeps them as direct siblings of the icon, which v4's adjacent-sibling rule in
   confirm.less needs, and reproduces the side-by-side layout with a grid: icon in column 1 across
   both rows, title and content in column 2. The icon's size and spacing come from v6's unscoped
   `.ant-modal-confirm .ant-modal-confirm-body > .anticon` rule. */
.ant-modal-confirm .ant-modal-confirm-body {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  row-gap: var(--ant-margin-xs);
  align-items: start;
}
.ant-modal-confirm .ant-modal-confirm-body > .anticon {
  grid-row: 1 / span 2;
  grid-column: 1;
}
.ant-modal-confirm .ant-modal-confirm-title,
.ant-modal-confirm .ant-modal-confirm-content {
  grid-column: 2;
  max-width: 100%;
}
/* Single-column variant, mirroring `.ant-modal-confirm-body-no-icon .ant-modal-confirm-paragraph
   { max-width: 100% }`. The confirm template always renders the icon today, so this is unused. */
.ant-modal-confirm .ant-modal-confirm-body-no-icon {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
}
.ant-modal-confirm .ant-modal-confirm-body-no-icon .ant-modal-confirm-title,
.ant-modal-confirm .ant-modal-confirm-body-no-icon .ant-modal-confirm-content {
  grid-column: 1;
}

/* Mirrors v6 `@media (max-width: 767px) { .ant-modal-root .ant-modal { max-width; margin }
   .ant-modal-root .ant-modal-centered .ant-modal { flex: 1 } }`: a narrow gutter on small screens. */
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .ant-modal {
    max-width: calc(100vw - 16px);
    margin: var(--ant-margin-xs) auto;
  }
  .ant-modal-centered .ant-modal {
    flex: 1;
  }
}
/* Motion, ported from components/notification/style/placement.less. v6's notification CSS is
   transition-based (rc-motion classes driven by --notification-y/-x) and defines no keyframes, but
   NzNotificationComponent adds ant-notification-fade-enter/-leave and removes the notice on
   `animationend`, so without these keyframes a notification is never removed. */
.ant-notification .ant-notification-fade-enter,
.ant-notification .ant-notification-fade-leave {
  animation-duration: var(--ant-motion-duration-mid);
  animation-timing-function: var(--ant-motion-ease-in-out);
  animation-fill-mode: both;
}
.ant-notification .ant-notification-fade-enter {
  animation-name: antNotificationFadeIn;
}
.ant-notification .ant-notification-fade-leave {
  animation-name: antNotificationFadeOut;
  /* v6 sets `overflow: visible` on the notice; the max-height collapse below only hides the content
     while it shrinks if the leaving notice clips it. */
  overflow: hidden;
}
.ant-notification.ant-notification-top .ant-notification-fade-enter {
  animation-name: antNotificationTopFadeIn;
}
.ant-notification.ant-notification-bottom .ant-notification-fade-enter {
  animation-name: antNotificationBottomFadeIn;
}
.ant-notification.ant-notification-topLeft .ant-notification-fade-enter,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-bottomLeft .ant-notification-fade-enter {
  animation-name: antNotificationLeftFadeIn;
}
@keyframes antNotificationFadeIn {
  0% {
    transform: translate3d(100%, 0, 0);
    opacity: 0;
  }
  100% {
    transform: translate3d(0, 0, 0);
    opacity: 1;
  }
}
@keyframes antNotificationTopFadeIn {
  0% {
    top: -150px;
    opacity: 0;
  }
  100% {
    top: 0;
    opacity: 1;
  }
}
@keyframes antNotificationBottomFadeIn {
  0% {
    bottom: -150px;
    opacity: 0;
  }
  100% {
    bottom: 0;
    opacity: 1;
  }
}
@keyframes antNotificationLeftFadeIn {
  0% {
    transform: translate3d(-100%, 0, 0);
    opacity: 0;
  }
  100% {
    transform: translate3d(0, 0, 0);
    opacity: 1;
  }
}
@keyframes antNotificationFadeOut {
  0% {
    max-height: 150px;
    /* The placement root's `gap` already spaces the notices; a start margin would add to it and
       snap back as the collapse runs. */
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }
  100% {
    max-height: 0;
    margin-block-end: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    opacity: 0;
  }
}

/* v6 `.ant-notification .ant-notification-notice { position: absolute }` assumes rc-notification's
   stacking, where JS offsets each notice with --notification-y. ng-zorro stacks the notices in normal
   flow, so they stay relative (same selector, wins on source order). */
.ant-notification .ant-notification-notice {
  position: relative;
}

/* Mirrors v6 `.ant-notification .ant-notification-list-content { gap }` and
   `.ant-notification.ant-notification-list { padding: var(--notification-margin-edge) }` (24px) onto
   ng-zorro's six placement roots, which render the notices directly, without the `-list` class or a
   `-list-content` holder. Only the inline padding is needed: the roots' inline top/bottom styles
   already carry nzTop/nzBottom. */
.ant-notification.ant-notification-topLeft,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-topRight,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-bottomLeft,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-bottomRight,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-top,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-bottom {
  gap: var(--ant-margin);
  padding-inline: var(--ant-margin-lg);
}

/* Mirrors v6 `.ant-notification.ant-notification-list { pointer-events: none; max-height: 100vh }`.
   The bare v6 `.ant-notification` root is a fixed, 100vh-tall box, and ng-zorro renders all six
   placement roots even when empty; without this they would intercept clicks on most of the page.
   The notices keep v6's own `pointer-events: auto`. */
.ant-notification.ant-notification-topLeft,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-topRight,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-bottomLeft,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-bottomRight,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-top,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-bottom {
  pointer-events: none;
  height: auto;
  max-height: 100vh;
}

/* v6 centres top/bottom notices with `left: 50%; transform: translate3d(-50%, 0, 0)` on the notice.
   ng-zorro's container already centres the whole `-top`/`-bottom` root inline, and the enter/leave
   keyframes above set their own `transform`, so the notice-level centring is cancelled. */
.ant-notification.ant-notification-top .ant-notification-notice,
.ant-notification.ant-notification-bottom .ant-notification-notice {
  left: auto;
  transform: none;
}

/* v6 lays the icon and a title/description column out as flex siblings in `-notice-wrapper` with
   `gap: var(--ant-margin-sm)`. ng-zorro keeps v4's flat structure (icon, title, description and
   actions are siblings in `-notice-section`), so the icon is taken out of flow and, as in v4, only
   a notice with an icon indents its text, by the icon size plus the same gap. */
.ant-notification-notice-icon {
  position: absolute;
}
.ant-notification-notice-with-icon .ant-notification-notice-title,
.ant-notification-notice-with-icon .ant-notification-notice-description {
  margin-inline-start: calc(var(--ant-notification-icon-font-size) + var(--ant-margin-sm));
}

/* v6 right-aligns `-notice-actions` with `float: right; margin-top: var(--ant-margin-sm)`. In
   ng-zorro the actions sit in v6's flex-column `-notice-section`, where `float` has no effect, so
   `align-self: flex-end` does the same job. */
.ant-notification-notice-section > .ant-notification-notice-actions {
  align-self: flex-end;
  margin-top: var(--ant-margin-sm);
}
nz-pagination {
  display: block;
}

/*
 * v6 marks the pager item adjacent to a jump control with `ant-pagination-item-after-jump-prev` /
 * `ant-pagination-item-before-jump-next` so the responsive rule below can hide it under 992px
 * (antd's own `Pagination.js` derives them from data, not a prop: @rc-component/pagination's
 * `Pagination.js` clones the first/last item of the freshly generated page range with the class
 * when `hasJumpPrev`/`hasJumpNext` is true). The compiled v4 CSS already selects both literal
 * classes at the same breakpoint (`publish/ng-zorro-antd.css`, the `@media (max-width: 992px)`
 * block right after the disabled-state rules), so they are not emitted; the adjacency to the
 * already-emitted `ant-pagination-jump-prev` / `ant-pagination-jump-next` classes gives the same
 * result without touching a v4-styled selector.
 */
@media (max-width: 992px) {
  .ant-pagination .ant-pagination-jump-prev + .ant-pagination-item,
  .ant-pagination .ant-pagination-item:has(+ .ant-pagination-jump-next) {
    display: none;
  }
}
/* CDK overlay pane positioning; v6's `position: absolute` on the popup root would collapse the
   pane to 0x0 inside the CDK overlay pane (which is itself positioned), mispositioning the bubble.
   Port of `style/patch.less`'s `.ant-popover { position: relative; }` rule (popconfirm's popup root
   also carries `ant-popover`), as in popover's and tooltip's v6 patch. */
.ant-popconfirm.ant-popover {
  position: relative;
}
/* CDK overlay pane positioning; v6's `position: absolute` would collapse the pane to 0x0 inside the
   CDK overlay pane (which is itself positioned), mispositioning the bubble. Port of `style/patch.less`,
   as in tooltip's v6 patch. */
.ant-popover {
  position: relative;
}
/*
 * antd v6's `.ant-radio` CSS draws the dot control itself (size, border, background, the dot as
 * `::after`) because rc-checkbox no longer renders a separate inner span; ng-zorro keeps that span as
 * `.ant-radio-inner` for the default v4 stylesheet. The rules below mirror `.ant-radio` /
 * `.ant-radio-checked` / `.ant-radio-disabled` from the extracted v6 CSS onto `.ant-radio-inner`, and the
 * outer `.ant-radio` box is neutralised so it is not drawn twice. The radio-button variant renders
 * `.ant-radio-button-inner` instead (see class-allowlist.json: v6 leaves it unstyled and relies on the
 * `.ant-radio-button-wrapper` background/border for the pill's appearance), so it is unaffected here.
 */
.ant-radio {
  width: auto;
  height: auto;
  background-color: transparent;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 0;
  outline: none;
}
.ant-radio::after {
  display: none;
}
/*
 * Every rule above is a bare `.ant-radio` reset, but v6 paints the box through selectors scoped under
 * `.ant-radio-wrapper` (two classes: 0,2,0), which outweighs a bare `.ant-radio` reset (0,1,0) regardless
 * of source order. Each reset below repeats the ancestor scope so it matches v6's specificity exactly
 * and wins on source order instead.
 */
.ant-radio-wrapper .ant-radio {
  width: auto;
  height: auto;
  background-color: transparent;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 0;
  outline: none;
}
.ant-radio-wrapper .ant-radio::after {
  display: none;
}
.ant-radio-wrapper .ant-radio:has(.ant-radio-input:focus-visible) {
  outline: none;
}
.ant-radio-wrapper:hover:not(.ant-radio-wrapper-disabled) .ant-radio {
  border-color: transparent;
}
.ant-radio-wrapper .ant-radio-checked,
.ant-radio-wrapper .ant-radio-disabled {
  background: transparent;
  border: none;
}
.ant-radio-wrapper:hover .ant-radio-checked:not(.ant-radio-disabled) {
  background-color: transparent;
  border-color: transparent;
}
.ant-radio-inner {
  position: relative;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  display: block;
  width: calc(var(--ant-radio-radio-size) * 1px);
  height: calc(var(--ant-radio-radio-size) * 1px);
  background-color: var(--ant-color-bg-container);
  border: var(--ant-line-width) var(--ant-line-type) var(--ant-color-border);
  border-radius: 50%;
  transition: all var(--ant-motion-duration-mid);
}
.ant-radio-inner::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(0);
  width: calc(var(--ant-radio-dot-size) * 1px);
  height: calc(var(--ant-radio-dot-size) * 1px);
  background-color: var(--ant-radio-radio-color);
  border-radius: 50%;
  transform-origin: 50% 50%;
  opacity: 0;
  transition: all var(--ant-motion-duration-slow) var(--ant-motion-ease-in-out-circ);
}
.ant-radio-wrapper:hover:not(.ant-radio-wrapper-disabled) .ant-radio:not(.ant-radio-disabled) .ant-radio-inner {
  border-color: var(--ant-color-primary);
}
.ant-radio-checked .ant-radio-inner {
  background-color: var(--ant-radio-radio-bg-color);
  border-color: var(--ant-color-primary);
}
.ant-radio-checked .ant-radio-inner::after {
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  opacity: 1;
}
.ant-radio-wrapper:hover .ant-radio-checked:not(.ant-radio-disabled) .ant-radio-inner {
  background-color: var(--ant-color-primary-hover);
  border-color: transparent;
}
.ant-radio-disabled .ant-radio-inner {
  background: var(--ant-color-bg-container-disabled);
  border-color: var(--ant-color-border);
}
.ant-radio-disabled .ant-radio-inner::after {
  background-color: var(--ant-radio-dot-color-disabled);
}
.ant-radio:has(.ant-radio-input:focus-visible) .ant-radio-inner {
  outline: var(--ant-line-width-focus) solid var(--ant-color-primary-border);
  outline-offset: 1px;
  transition:
    outline-offset 0s,
    outline 0s;
}

/* style/patch.less: hides the trailing label span when the projected content is empty. */
.ant-radio + span:empty {
  display: none;
}
nz-result {
  display: block;
}
/*
 * antd v6's rc-select no longer renders a separate selector box: `SelectInput`'s root *is* the
 * select root, and the box (border, radius, height, background, padding — antd's bare `.ant-select`
 * rule) is drawn on it directly. ng-zorro keeps `nz-select-top-control` (`.ant-select-selector`) as
 * a nested box, matching v4's own architecture where `.ant-select` never carries a border and
 * `.ant-select-selector` does. Mirror the box onto `.ant-select-selector`, reading the same custom
 * properties antd's `.ant-select` rule sets (they inherit from the root ancestor), and neutralise
 * the paint (not layout) properties that would otherwise double the box on the root.
 */
.ant-select {
  border: none;
  background: transparent;
  padding-inline: 0;
  padding-block: 0;
  border-radius: 0;
}
.ant-select .ant-select-selector {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  width: 100%;
  height: var(--ant-select-height);
  padding-inline: var(--ant-select-padding-horizontal);
  padding-block: var(--ant-select-padding-vertical);
  border-width: var(--ant-select-border-size);
  border-style: var(--ant-line-type);
  border-color: var(--ant-select-border-color);
  border-radius: var(--ant-select-border-radius);
  background: var(--ant-select-background-color);
  transition: all var(--ant-motion-duration-slow);
  cursor: pointer;
}
.ant-select .ant-select-selector input {
  cursor: pointer;
}

/*
 * A select (or cascader, which carries the same `ant-select ant-select-single` root classes) inside an input
 * addon: antd's `.ant-input-group .ant-input-group-addon .ant-select.ant-select-single:not(.ant-select-customize-input):not(.ant-pagination-size-changer)`
 * rule (`background-color: inherit; border: 1px transparent; box-shadow: none`) removes the box from the
 * root, where antd draws it. Here the box is `.ant-select-selector`, so the same rule is mirrored onto it,
 * and the root's transparent border, which outranks `.ant-select { border: none }` above, is removed at
 * the same specificity so the control keeps the height of one border, not two. The root keeps antd's
 * inherited background. Input's own addon demo relies on this rule, shipped with select's styles.
 */
.ant-input-group
  .ant-input-group-addon
  .ant-select.ant-select-single:not(.ant-select-customize-input):not(.ant-pagination-size-changer) {
  border: none;
}
.ant-input-group
  .ant-input-group-addon
  .ant-select.ant-select-single:not(.ant-select-customize-input):not(.ant-pagination-size-changer)
  .ant-select-selector {
  background-color: transparent;
  border: var(--ant-line-width) var(--ant-line-type) transparent;
  box-shadow: none;
}
.ant-select-show-search .ant-select-selector,
.ant-select-show-search .ant-select-selector input {
  cursor: text;
}
.ant-select-disabled .ant-select-selector {
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

/*
 * `.ant-select-disabled` paints its background as a real `background` property directly (not
 * through `--ant-select-background-color`, which the box mirror above reads) — it is not
 * reachable through the generic mirror at all, and it is also masked on the (already-neutralised)
 * root by the unconditional `.ant-select { background: transparent }` above. Mirror it explicitly.
 */
.ant-select.ant-select-disabled .ant-select-selector {
  background: var(--ant-color-bg-container-disabled);
}

/*
 * antd v6 draws the focus ring as a real `box-shadow` on the root, only for the outlined variant
 * (default, -status-error, -status-warning): `.ant-select.ant-select-outlined:not(.ant-select-disabled).ant-select-focused`
 * and its status siblings. The equivalent filled/borderless/underlined focused rules also set a
 * real `box-shadow` on the root, but always to `transparent` — a no-op regardless of the root's
 * shape, so they need no neutralising or mirroring. Borderless's focus ring is a native `outline`
 * on `:has(input:focus-visible)`, which already draws correctly on the root here: with the root's
 * own border/background/padding neutralised above and the select-clear/-arrow siblings taken out
 * of flow (`position: absolute`), the root's `inline-flex` box is exactly the size of
 * `.ant-select-selector`, so the outline needs no separate mirror either. Only the three outlined
 * rules paint a real, non-transparent shadow that would otherwise land on the invisible root.
 */
.ant-select.ant-select-outlined:not(.ant-select-disabled).ant-select-focused,
.ant-select.ant-select-outlined.ant-select-status-error:not(.ant-select-disabled).ant-select-focused,
.ant-select.ant-select-outlined.ant-select-status-warning:not(.ant-select-disabled).ant-select-focused {
  box-shadow: none;
}
.ant-select.ant-select-outlined:not(.ant-select-disabled).ant-select-focused .ant-select-selector {
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--ant-control-outline-width) var(--ant-select-active-outline-color);
}
.ant-select.ant-select-outlined.ant-select-status-error:not(.ant-select-disabled).ant-select-focused
  .ant-select-selector {
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--ant-control-outline-width) var(--ant-color-error-outline);
}
.ant-select.ant-select-outlined.ant-select-status-warning:not(.ant-select-disabled).ant-select-focused
  .ant-select-selector {
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--ant-control-outline-width) var(--ant-color-warning-outline);
}

/*
 * `.ant-select-underlined` removes the top/side borders and the corner radius as real properties
 * (not through the `--ant-select-border-radius`/`-border-color` variables the box mirror reads),
 * always, not only when focused. Mirror them.
 */
.ant-select-underlined .ant-select-selector {
  border-radius: 0;
  border-top-color: transparent;
  border-inline-color: transparent;
}

/*
 * antd v6 has no equivalent of the `.ant-select-selection-wrap` span (its `.ant-select-prefix`,
 * `.ant-select-content` and `.ant-select-suffix` sit directly under the select root); port the
 * positioning v4's own mixin gives it (`components/select/style/index.less` `.select-selector()`
 * `-selection-wrap` block) so `.ant-select-selection-placeholder`, which positions itself relative
 * to its nearest positioned ancestor, still has a sized, positioned one under the v6 theme.
 */
.ant-select-selector .ant-select-selection-wrap {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
}

/*
 * antd v6 folds the trailing icon into `.ant-select-suffix`, an `Affix` that is a flex sibling of
 * `.ant-select-content` under the select root; ng-zorro keeps `nz-select-arrow` as its own
 * absolutely positioned sibling of `.ant-select-selector`, as v4's own `&-arrow` rule does. Port
 * that positioning with v6 tokens, since no v6 CSS rule targets `.ant-select-arrow` at all.
 */
/*
 * In antd the suffix is an in-flow flex item (`flex: none`, `font-size: var(--ant-font-size-icon)`) after
 * `.ant-select-content`, whose `margin-inline-end` (show-arrow padding minus the icon size) is only the gap
 * before it. With the arrow taken out of flow here, reserve the icon's width at the end of the content, or a
 * content-sized select (e.g. in an input addon) draws its arrow over the selected text.
 */
.ant-select-show-arrow .ant-select-selector .ant-select-selection-wrap {
  padding-inline-end: var(--ant-font-size-icon);
}
.ant-select .ant-select-arrow {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  inset-inline-end: var(--ant-select-padding-horizontal);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  height: var(--ant-font-size-icon);
  margin-top: calc(var(--ant-font-size-icon) * -1 / 2);
  color: var(--ant-color-text-quaternary);
  font-size: var(--ant-font-size-icon);
  line-height: 1;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.ant-select-disabled .ant-select-arrow {
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

/*
 * antd v6 sizes the multiple-mode search input via a `--select-input-width` custom property that
 * its own JS writes as an inline style on the input; ng-zorro measures width with a hidden mirror
 * element instead (`NzSelectSearchComponent.syncMirrorWidth`) and has no code path that writes
 * `--select-input-width`. Port the mirror-driven sizing v4's own `multiple.less`
 * `.@{select-prefix-cls}-selection-search` block gives it, with v6 tokens, so the input has a
 * width at all under the v6 theme.
 */
.ant-select-multiple .ant-select-content .ant-select-selection-search {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-flex;
  max-width: 100%;
}
.ant-select-multiple .ant-select-content .ant-select-selection-search-input,
.ant-select-multiple .ant-select-content .ant-select-selection-search-mirror {
  height: var(--ant-select-multi-item-height);
  line-height: var(--ant-select-multi-item-height);
  transition: all var(--ant-motion-duration-slow);
}
.ant-select-multiple .ant-select-content .ant-select-selection-search-input {
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 4.1px;
}
.ant-select-multiple .ant-select-content .ant-select-selection-search-mirror {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 999;
  white-space: pre;
  visibility: hidden;
  inset-inline-start: 0;
  inset-inline-end: auto;
}

/* antd positions popups with inline styles from rc-trigger; ng-zorro positions the CDK overlay pane instead. */
.ant-select-dropdown {
  position: relative;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
}
.ant-select-dropdown .cdk-virtual-scroll-content-wrapper {
  right: 0;
}
.ant-select-dropdown .full-width {
  contain: initial;
}
.ant-select-dropdown .full-width .cdk-virtual-scroll-content-wrapper {
  position: static;
}
.ant-select-dropdown .full-width .cdk-virtual-scroll-spacer {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  width: 1px;
}
/* ng-zorro's `nz-slider` host is the `.ant-slider` element; v4's `style/patch.less` makes it a block box. */
.ant-slider {
  display: block;
}

/*
 * antd's `.ant-slider .ant-slider-mark-text-active { color: var(--ant-color-text) }`, keyed onto the active
 * mark's existing `ant-slider-mark-active` class: the v4 stylesheet also styles `ant-slider-mark-text-active`
 * (darker active marks), so emitting it would change the default theme.
 */
.ant-slider .ant-slider-mark-active {
  color: var(--ant-color-text);
}
nz-space-item {
  display: block;
}
/* patch.less: nz-spin { display: block } */
nz-spin {
  display: block;
}

/* mirrors antd v6 `.ant-spin.ant-spin-section,.ant-spin >.ant-spin-section` (flex layout + primary
   colour) and `.ant-spin >.ant-spin-section` (absolute centering) for ng-zorro's nested structure
   (`.ant-spin-nested-loading > div > .ant-spin`), where ng-zorro's inner `.ant-spin` plays the role
   v6 gives its `.ant-spin-section` child: it holds the indicator + description and is centered over
   the sibling `.ant-spin-container`. */
.ant-spin-nested-loading > div > .ant-spin {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  inset-inline-start: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  z-index: 1;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--ant-padding-sm);
  color: var(--ant-color-primary);
}

/* mirrors antd v6 `.ant-spin .ant-spin-container` */
.ant-spin-nested-loading .ant-spin-container {
  position: relative;
  transition: opacity var(--ant-motion-duration-slow);
}

/* mirrors antd v6 `.ant-spin .ant-spin-container::after` */
.ant-spin-nested-loading .ant-spin-container::after {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  inset-inline-end: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  inset-inline-start: 0;
  z-index: 10;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: var(--ant-color-bg-container);
  opacity: 0;
  transition: all var(--ant-motion-duration-slow);
  content: '';
  pointer-events: none;
}

/* mirrors antd v6 `.ant-spin-spinning .ant-spin-container` onto ng-zorro's v4-compat `.ant-spin-blur` */
.ant-spin-container.ant-spin-blur {
  clear: both;
  opacity: 0.5;
  user-select: none;
  pointer-events: none;
}

/* mirrors antd v6 `.ant-spin-spinning .ant-spin-container::after` */
.ant-spin-container.ant-spin-blur::after {
  opacity: 0.4;
  pointer-events: auto;
}
/* Port of splitter/style/patch.less: the nz-splitter host is a custom element (inline by default);
   .ant-splitter's display:flex applies once the class is present, this covers the host before. */
nz-splitter {
  display: block;
}
/*
 * The title box is rendered unconditionally (statistic.component.ts) so the compiled v4 CSS's
 * `.ant-statistic-title { margin-bottom: 4px }` still applies to a title-less statistic. v6's own
 * Statistic.js skips the header entirely when there is no title, so under the v6 bundle alone the
 * always-present, empty header would otherwise keep its `.ant-statistic .ant-statistic-header
 * { padding-bottom: var(--ant-margin-xxs) }` band (publish/style/v6/template.css) with nothing in
 * it. Hiding it here, keyed on the title div being empty, reaches the v6-only result without
 * touching the v4 DOM.
 */
.ant-statistic-header:has(> .ant-statistic-title:empty) {
  display: none;
}
/*
 * ng-zorro's step keeps its v4 element tree for the default stylesheet:
 *
 *   nz-step.ant-steps-item
 *     div.ant-steps-item-container.ant-steps-item-wrapper   (role="button" when clickable)
 *       div.ant-steps-item-tail.ant-steps-item-rail          (not on the last step)
 *       div.ant-steps-item-icon > span.ant-steps-icon | div.ant-steps-progress-icon
 *       div.ant-steps-item-content.ant-steps-item-section
 *         div.ant-steps-item-title > div.ant-steps-item-subtitle
 *         div.ant-steps-item-description
 *
 * antd v6 renders `-item-wrapper > (-item-icon, -item-section > (-item-header > (-item-title,
 * -item-subtitle, -item-rail), -item-content))` with `role="button"` on the item. The v4 stylesheet
 * pairs `.ant-steps-item-content > .ant-steps-item-title` and `.ant-steps-item-container >
 * .ant-steps-item-tail` with child combinators, so no header element is inserted and the rail stays
 * the wrapper's first child. The rules below carry antd's header rules onto the title, antd's body
 * (`-item-content`) rules onto the description, antd's item-level clickable rules onto the wrapper
 * that holds the role, and place the rail after the title where antd's rail sits in flow.
 */

/* Header: antd `.ant-steps .ant-steps-item-header`; the title element also holds the subtitle. */
.ant-steps .ant-steps-item-section > .ant-steps-item-title {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: nowrap;
  align-items: center;
}

/* antd `.ant-steps-title-horizontal .ant-steps-item-header` */
.ant-steps-title-horizontal .ant-steps-item-section > .ant-steps-item-title {
  min-height: var(--ant-cmp-steps-heading-height);
}

/* antd `.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-vertical .ant-steps-item-empty-header .ant-steps-item-header` */
.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-vertical .ant-steps-item-empty-header .ant-steps-item-section > .ant-steps-item-title {
  min-height: auto;
}

/* antd `.ant-steps-title-vertical > .ant-steps-item .ant-steps-item-header` */
.ant-steps-title-vertical > .ant-steps-item .ant-steps-item-section > .ant-steps-item-title {
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
}

/*
 * Body text: antd's `-item-content` is the description slot, while ng-zorro's `-item-content` is the
 * section (the v4 name). The description carries antd's body rules; antd's
 * `.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-vertical .ant-steps-item-empty-header .ant-steps-item-content`
 * margin is not repeated here because it already lands on the section above the description.
 */
/* antd `.ant-steps .ant-steps-item-content` (base and status colour rules) */
.ant-steps .ant-steps-item-description {
  color: var(--ant-cmp-steps-item-content-color);
  font-size: var(--ant-font-size);
  line-height: var(--ant-line-height);
  word-break: break-word;
  transition: all var(--ant-motion-duration-slow);
}

/* antd `.ant-steps .ant-steps-item-active .ant-steps-item-content` */
.ant-steps .ant-steps-item-active .ant-steps-item-description {
  color: var(--ant-cmp-steps-item-content-active-color);
}

/* antd `.ant-steps-title-horizontal .ant-steps-item-content` */
.ant-steps-title-horizontal .ant-steps-item-description {
  max-width: var(--ant-steps-description-max-width);
}

/* antd's description width cap must not narrow the section that shares the `-item-content` name. */
.ant-steps-title-horizontal .ant-steps-item-content.ant-steps-item-section {
  max-width: none;
}

/* antd `.ant-steps-title-vertical > .ant-steps-item .ant-steps-item-content` */
.ant-steps-title-vertical > .ant-steps-item .ant-steps-item-description {
  text-align: center;
  max-width: 100%;
}

/* antd `.ant-steps.ant-steps-navigation.ant-steps-vertical .ant-steps-item…ant-steps-item .ant-steps-item-content` */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-navigation.ant-steps-vertical .ant-steps-item.ant-steps-item.ant-steps-item.ant-steps-item .ant-steps-item-description {
  padding: 0;
}

/*
 * Rail in flow (horizontal steps with titles beside the icon): antd draws the rail inside the header,
 * after the title, as a flex item that fills the rest of the row. Here the rail is the wrapper's first
 * child, so the wrapper becomes a grid: icon | title (header) | rail on the first row, the description
 * under title and rail, and the section lets its children join the grid. The icon's end margin stands
 * in for antd's wrapper `column-gap` (`.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-horizontal
 * .ant-steps-item-wrapper`), which would otherwise also open between title and rail. Every other
 * layout positions the rail absolutely against the item, which works from the wrapper unchanged.
 * Navigation steps hide the rail and keep antd's flex wrapper.
 */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-horizontal:not(.ant-steps-navigation) .ant-steps-item-wrapper {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, max-content) minmax(0, 1fr);
  column-gap: 0;
}

.ant-steps.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-horizontal:not(.ant-steps-navigation) .ant-steps-item-wrapper > .ant-steps-item-icon {
  grid-column: 1;
  grid-row: 1 / span 2;
  margin-inline-end: var(--ant-margin-xs);
}

.ant-steps.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-horizontal:not(.ant-steps-navigation) .ant-steps-item-wrapper > .ant-steps-item-section {
  display: contents;
}

.ant-steps.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-horizontal:not(.ant-steps-navigation) .ant-steps-item-section > .ant-steps-item-title {
  grid-column: 2;
  grid-row: 1;
}

.ant-steps.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-horizontal:not(.ant-steps-navigation) .ant-steps-item-section > .ant-steps-item-description {
  grid-column: 2 / -1;
  grid-row: 2;
}

.ant-steps.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-horizontal:not(.ant-steps-navigation) .ant-steps-item-wrapper > .ant-steps-item-rail {
  grid-column: 3;
  grid-row: 1;
}

/*
 * nzEllipsis: the title's track is sized to `max-content` above so the title never needs to shrink;
 * with `ant-steps-ellipsis` the track becomes flexible (and the title's own grid-item minimum, which
 * defaults to its content size, is cleared) so the `overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis` that
 * antd's own `.ant-steps.ant-steps-ellipsis .ant-steps-item-title` rule sets can actually truncate it.
 */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-ellipsis.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-horizontal:not(.ant-steps-navigation) .ant-steps-item-wrapper {
  grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
}

.ant-steps.ant-steps-ellipsis.ant-steps-title-horizontal.ant-steps-horizontal:not(.ant-steps-navigation) .ant-steps-item-section > .ant-steps-item-title {
  min-width: 0;
}

/*
 * Clickable steps: antd puts `role="button"` on the item; ng-zorro puts it on the wrapper, so antd's
 * `.ant-steps-item[role='button']` rules match the item that holds such a wrapper.
 */
/*
 * antd `.ant-steps .ant-steps-item[role='button']:focus-visible`: the ring goes around the item (which
 * is wider than the wrapper in navigation steps and taller in vertical ones), not around the focused
 * wrapper, whose own UA ring is suppressed.
 */
.ant-steps .ant-steps-item:has(> .ant-steps-item-wrapper[role='button']:focus-visible) {
  outline: var(--ant-line-width-focus) solid var(--ant-color-primary-border);
  outline-offset: 1px;
  transition:
    outline-offset 0s,
    outline 0s;
}

.ant-steps .ant-steps-item-wrapper[role='button']:focus-visible {
  outline: none;
}

/* antd `.ant-steps .ant-steps-item[role='button']:not(.ant-steps-item-active):hover` */
.ant-steps .ant-steps-item:has(> .ant-steps-item-wrapper[role='button']):not(.ant-steps-item-active):hover {
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* antd `.ant-steps .ant-steps-item[role='button']:not(.ant-steps-item-active):hover .ant-steps-item-title, … .ant-steps-item-content` */
.ant-steps .ant-steps-item:has(> .ant-steps-item-wrapper[role='button']):not(.ant-steps-item-active):hover .ant-steps-item-title,
.ant-steps .ant-steps-item:has(> .ant-steps-item-wrapper[role='button']):not(.ant-steps-item-active):hover .ant-steps-item-description {
  color: var(--ant-cmp-steps-item-text-hover-color);
}

/* antd `.ant-steps:not(.ant-steps-dot) .ant-steps-item:not(.ant-steps-item-custom)[role='button']:not(.ant-steps-item-active):hover .ant-steps-item-icon` */
.ant-steps:not(.ant-steps-dot) .ant-steps-item:not(.ant-steps-item-custom):has(> .ant-steps-item-wrapper[role='button']):not(.ant-steps-item-active):hover .ant-steps-item-icon {
  background: var(--ant-cmp-steps-item-icon-bg-hover-color);
  border-color: var(--ant-cmp-steps-item-icon-border-hover-color);
  color: var(--ant-cmp-steps-item-icon-text-hover-color);
}

/*
 * Dot style: antd paints the dot on `.ant-steps-item-icon` itself and widens its hit area with
 * `.ant-steps.ant-steps-dot .ant-steps-item-icon:after`; antd's custom dot render wraps that icon. A
 * custom `nzProgressDot` template wraps ng-zorro's inner `.ant-steps-icon-dot` instead, so the inner
 * span takes the same hit area (it paints nothing) and the dot fills it whatever the template's own
 * wrapper does, keeping the template's hover target where the dot is.
 */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-dot .ant-steps-item-icon > .ant-steps-icon {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  width: var(--ant-steps-icon-size);
  height: var(--ant-steps-icon-size);
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  /* above the icon's own `::after`, which comes later in paint order and would take the hover */
  z-index: 1;
}

.ant-steps.ant-steps-dot .ant-steps-item-icon .ant-steps-icon-dot {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
}

/*
 * Progress ring: ng-zorro composes `nz-progress` inside `.ant-steps-progress-icon` where antd draws
 * its own SVG. The wrapper takes the box and the sizing variables of antd's
 * `.ant-steps.ant-steps-with-progress .ant-steps-item-progress-icon-svg` (the icon's padding box plus
 * two bold line widths on every side; the variables are declared on antd's SVG class only).
 */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-with-progress .ant-steps-progress-icon {
  --ant-cmp-steps-svg-size: calc(
    calc(var(--ant-line-width-bold) + var(--ant-line-width-bold)) * 2 + var(--ant-cmp-steps-icon-size)
  );
  --ant-cmp-steps-icon-size-ptg-unitless: calc(100 / tan(atan2(var(--ant-cmp-steps-svg-size), 1px)));
  position: absolute;
  inset: calc(calc(var(--ant-line-width-bold) + var(--ant-line-width-bold)) * -1);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  line-height: 0;
}

/*
 * `nz-progress` sizes its circle with an inline 40px / 32px box; the static inner box lets the SVG fill
 * the wrapper instead (beats progress' `.ant-progress-circle .ant-progress-body{position:relative}`).
 */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-with-progress .ant-steps-progress-icon .ant-progress-inner {
  position: static;
}

.ant-steps.ant-steps-with-progress .ant-steps-progress-icon svg.ant-progress-circle {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  overflow: visible;
}

/*
 * antd `.ant-steps.ant-steps-with-progress .ant-steps-item-progress-icon-circle`: stroke in viewBox
 * units that renders as `lineWidthBold`, butt caps; CSS overrides `nz-progress`'s presentation
 * attributes.
 */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-with-progress .ant-steps-progress-icon .ant-progress-circle-path,
.ant-steps.ant-steps-with-progress .ant-steps-progress-icon .ant-progress-circle-trail {
  stroke-width: calc(var(--ant-cmp-steps-icon-size-ptg-unitless) * var(--ant-line-width-bold));
  stroke-linecap: butt;
}

/* antd `.ant-steps.ant-steps-with-progress .ant-steps-item-progress-icon-circle-rail` */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-with-progress .ant-steps-progress-icon .ant-progress-circle-trail {
  stroke: var(--ant-color-split);
}

/*
 * Inline: antd `.ant-steps-inline .ant-steps-item-content { display: none }` hides antd's body slot; ng-zorro's
 * section carries that v4 name, so the section is shown again and the description hidden instead.
 */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-inline .ant-steps-item-content.ant-steps-item-section {
  display: block;
}
.ant-steps.ant-steps-inline .ant-steps-item-description {
  display: none;
}
/* antd `.ant-steps.ant-steps-panel .ant-steps-item-header { min-height: auto }`, onto the title. */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-panel .ant-steps-item-section > .ant-steps-item-title {
  min-height: auto;
}
/*
 * The arrow carries `display="none"` so that it is inert without this stylesheet; the presentation attribute
 * loses to this rule, and antd's `.ant-steps-item:last-child .ant-steps-panel-arrow` still hides the last one.
 */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-panel .ant-steps-panel-arrow {
  display: block;
}
/* antd `.ant-steps.ant-steps-ellipsis .ant-steps-item-content` body rule, onto the description. */
.ant-steps.ant-steps-ellipsis .ant-steps-item-description {
  overflow: hidden;
  white-space: nowrap;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}
nz-switch {
  display: inline-block;
}
/*
 * Angular custom elements have no default display; v4's `style/patch.less` sets `display: block`
 * (or `inline-flex` for the filter trigger) for ng-zorro's own table elements so they lay out like
 * the plain HTML/antd DOM they stand in for. This is not antd-specific (it is needed regardless of
 * which theme's CSS is loaded), so it is ported as-is rather than tied to any v6 token.
 */
nz-table,
nz-table-title-footer,
nz-table-inner-scroll,
nz-table-inner-default,
nz-table-selection {
  display: block;
}

nz-filter-trigger {
  display: inline-flex;
}

/*
 * `nzOuterBordered` (`.nz-table-out-bordered`) is an ng-zorro-only input with no antd equivalent:
 * it draws the same border antd v6's `.ant-table-bordered` uses (`--ant-table-border-color`) around
 * the title/container/footer instead of every cell. Ported from v4's rule with v6 tokens.
 */
.nz-table-out-bordered > .ant-table-title {
  border: var(--ant-line-width) var(--ant-line-type) var(--ant-table-border-color);
  border-bottom: 0;
}
.nz-table-out-bordered > .ant-table-container {
  border: var(--ant-line-width) var(--ant-line-type) var(--ant-table-border-color);
  border-bottom: 0;
}
.nz-table-out-bordered > .ant-table-footer {
  border: var(--ant-line-width) var(--ant-line-type) var(--ant-table-border-color);
  border-top: 0;
}

/* CDK's virtual-scroll viewport (ng-zorro's `nzVirtualScroll`) is not antd's own scroller, so v6
 * has no rule for it; v4's own scrollbar fix is ported unchanged (no antd token involved). */
cdk-virtual-scroll-viewport.ant-table-body {
  overflow-y: scroll;
}

/* The fixed table header's own scrollbar is hidden so only the body's is visible; the header's
 * background is read from the v6 token so both scrollbar and the row behind it match. */
.nz-table-hide-scrollbar {
  scrollbar-color: var(--ant-table-header-bg) var(--ant-table-header-bg);
}
.nz-table-hide-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar {
  background-color: var(--ant-table-header-bg);
}

/*
 * antd v6 does not vary the header background by size the way v4 did (`@table-header-bg-sm`); its
 * token set has one `--ant-table-header-bg` for every size, so the small-table override is dropped
 * (not "kept as v4-compat" - there is nothing left to override).
 */

/*
 * Bordered + CDK virtual scroll: antd v6's own `bordered.js` walks `.ant-table-container >` the
