/*
 * antd v6 highlights a hovered row by toggling a JS-driven `ant-table-cell-row-hover` class on
 * every cell of the hovered row (`@rc-component/table` `Cell/index.js`'s `useHoverState`, so a
 * row-spanned cell lights up with the row it visually belongs to); the generated template CSS has
 * no plain `:hover` rule at all (checked `components/core/theme/generated/test-css.ts`:
 * `.ant-table-wrapper .ant-table-tbody .ant-table-row >.ant-table-cell-row-hover{background:...}`
 * is the only row-hover selector). ng-zorro does not track per-row hover state in JS, so this
 * mirrors the same background onto v4's plain `:hover` pseudo-class instead of adding the class -
 * a cheaper, additive equivalent for every table that does not rowSpan across the hovered row.
 */
.ant-table-tbody > tr.ant-table-row:hover > td {
  background: var(--ant-table-row-hover-bg);
  transition: background var(--ant-motion-duration-slow);
}
/*
 * No selected-row hover mirror: ng-zorro's table never emits `ant-table-row-selected` at all
 * (checked `components/table/src/**`), so there is no selected row for a `-selected:hover` rule to
 * apply to here.
 */

/*
 * v4's fixed-column scroll shadow is a container pseudo-element keyed off `ant-table-ping-left/
 * -right`; v6 moved it onto the boundary cell itself (`.ant-table-cell-fix-start/-end-shadow-show`,
 * toggled in `NzTableInnerScrollComponent.setScrollPositionClassName` alongside the v4 ping
 * classes), which the generated template CSS already renders (see
 * `node_modules/antd/es/table/style/fixed.js`). No patch rule is needed for the shadow itself; this
 * comment records that the ping classes now drive two things instead of one.
 */

/*
 * antd v6's `bordered.js` draws an extra separator on the FIRST fixed-right cell
 * (`.ant-table-cell-fix-right-first:not(.ant-table-cell-fix-right-last)::after{border-inline-end}`)
 * to avoid a doubled border when there are 2+ fixed-right columns (the comment in that source file
 * reads "Only add separator border when there are multiple fixed-right columns ... otherwise the
 * ::after border doubles up with the cell's own borderInlineEnd"). `@rc-component/table`'s own
 * `Cell/index.js` never emits `-fix-right-last` under its current v6 naming at all (only
 * `-fix-start`/`-fix-end`/`-fix-start-shadow`/`-fix-end-shadow`/their `-show` siblings) - `-right-
 * first`/`-right-last` survive only as v4-era compat selectors in the STYLE files. ng-zorro's own
 * `-right-first` is the v4-compat hook kept next to the real `ant-table-cell-fix-end` (see the
 * class-mapping table), but ng-zorro never computes a `-right-last` class at all (adding it would
 * turn on an existing v4 rule - `v4-rule-guard.spec.ts` catches this), so this selector's `:not(
 * .ant-table-cell-fix-right-last)` is unconditionally true for every fixed-right table ng-zorro
 * renders: the "only when multiple columns" guard never actually applies, and the extra border
 * shows up even on a single fixed-right column, doubling up with that cell's own
 * `border-inline-end` from the general bordered-cell rule. Neutralised below at equal specificity
 * (same selector list, same declaration property, patch.css source order after template.css wins
 * the tie) rather than emitting `-right-last` to make the real condition expressible.
 */
